---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SystemDiagram from '../components/diagrams/SystemDiagram.astro';
import {MODEL_SPECS} from '../data/model-specs';
import {SITE_URL} from '../config/site';
const steps=[['01','Define your backup needs','Choose the circuits and equipment you need during an outage.','/guides/first-time-buyer-guide/'],['02','Build a load plan','Use nameplate running and starting requirements.','/planning/sizing/'],['03','Understand the fuel supply','Compare consumption, local prices and outage constraints.','/planning/fuel/'],['04','Compare exact configurations','Check fuel-specific output, transfer equipment and evidence gaps.','/models/'],['05','Understand installation','Plan site assessment, utility coordination and approvals.','/installation/what-to-expect/'],['06','Compare three proposals','Make missing scope visible before comparing totals.','/planning/quotes/'],['07','Plan ownership','Budget maintenance, fuel, monitoring and repairs.','/planning/ownership/']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Plan Your Home Standby Generator with Evidence" description="Independent purchase planning for US homeowners: exact generator models, sizing, fuel, installed costs and a three-quote comparison. Sources and uncertainty made clear." schema={{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebSite',name:'HomeGeneratorGuide',url:SITE_URL+'/'}}>
<section class="publication-hero"><div class="editorial-container hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT RESEARCH · US HOMEOWNERS</p><h1>A better generator decision starts before the dealer call.</h1><p class="lede">Plan a major home backup-power investment: what needs power, what the equipment actually specifies, and what an installation quote leaves out.</p><div class="planner-actions"><a class="button" href="/planning/sizing/">Start generator sizing →</a><a class="button secondary" href="/planning/quotes/">Compare installer quotes</a></div></div><aside class="research-note"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT YOU CAN CHECK HERE</p><h2>Evidence you can follow.</h2><p>Manufacturer facts, planning assumptions and unresolved questions are kept separate. Every exact-model record links to its sources.</p><dl><div><dt>{MODEL_SPECS.length}</dt><dd>exact configurations, including package variants</dd></div><div><dt>5</dt><dd>manufacturers covered; depth varies</dd></div><div><dt>4</dt><dd>tools for load, fuel, quotes and ownership</dd></div></dl><p class="help">Research-based guidance. No hands-on generator testing. Technical professional review pending.</p><a href="/review-process/">How our review process works →</a></aside></div></section>
<section class="editorial-container publication-section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR PURCHASE PLAN</p><h2>Seven decisions. One coherent plan.</h2><p>Start where you are. Bring the results to a qualified installer for a property-specific assessment.</p></div><ol class="journey-list">{steps.map(([n,title,description,href])=><li><span aria-hidden="true">{n}</span><div><h3><a href={href}>{title} →</a></h3><p>{description}</p></div></li>)}</ol></section>
<section class="publication-band"><div class="editorial-container split-feature"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE SYSTEM, NOT JUST THE BOX</p><h2>Generator size is only one part of the purchase.</h2><p>Transfer equipment, managed loads, fuel capacity and installation scope determine what the system can support. A “whole-house” label does not settle those questions.</p><ul class="editorial-links"><li><a href="/installation/automatic-transfer-switch-guide/">Understand ATS and load management →</a></li><li><a href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/">Understand installed cost →</a></li><li><a href="/brands/">Compare generator brands →</a></li><li><a href="/models/">Browse exact models →</a></li></ul></div><SystemDiagram/></div></section>
<section class="editorial-container publication-section"><div class="split-feature"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE QUOTE DESK</p><h2>Compare the work behind the price.</h2><p>Put three proposals side by side. Identify missing fuel work, utility coordination, accessories and warranty scope. Add your own documented adjustments without pretending that the lowest price is automatically the best proposal.</p><a class="button" href="/planning/quotes/">Open the three-quote comparison →</a></div><div class="research-note"><h3>Before you sign, ask:</h3><ul class="editorial-links"><li>What is the exact generator and ATS model?</li><li>Which loads are backed up, and which must wait?</li><li>Who pays for gas capacity or electrical upgrades?</li><li>What is excluded from installation and service?</li></ul><a href="/cost/standby-generator-quote-checklist/">Read the full quote checklist →</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
